<title>USA: Video Lottery Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>Video Lottery Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							  March 31,</p>
<p> INCOME STATEMENT DATA:			  1997	   1996</p>
<p> Total						48,004	 44,745</p>
<p> Cost and expenses				46,258	 48,820</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss) before income</p>
<p>  taxes and extraordinary items		  987	(4,819)</p>
<p> Income taxes (expense) benefit		(703)	    985</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss) before extraordinary</p>
<p>  items						  284	(3,834)</p>
<p> Extraordinary gain			     13,269	  4,014</p>
<p> Net earnings				     13,553	    477</p>
<p>Per share net earnings (loss):</p>
<p>  from continuing operations		     .03	  (.30)</p>
<p>  from discontinued operations		    --	    .02</p>
<p>  from extraordinary items			1.26	    .32</p>
<p> Total						  1.29	    .04</p>
<p> Weighted average common shares	 10,498,000   12,601,000</p>
<p>(In thousands except for per share data and number of shares)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Average shares outstanding exclude common stock equivalents if antidilutive.</p>
<p>Net income for the first quarter of 1997 includes an extraordinary gain (net of tax) of $13.3 million ($1.26 per common and common equivalent share) resulting from the settlement in January of all outstanding litigation, claims and disputes with Electronic Data Systems Corp.</p>
<p>Net income for the first quarter of 1996 include an extraordinary gain of $4.0 million (net of tax) related to a settlement with the sellers of United Wagering Systems, acquired by Video Lottery in 1994, and $6.0 million of special charges.</p>
</text>
